+# Instruction and revision checklist
+
+- [x] Compare requested 336/337 against 326/636/637/639: completed in commit 385f959fd70d5caee75fe192325771ed7d8bdc9d; linked without rewriting it. Source details and conflicts remain there.
+- [x] Preserve original records and conflicting values: no source or prior document altered; September 18 unconfirmed/all-OK/fax accounts retained together.
+- [x] Continue available operational-record work: pages 19–24 checked within prospectively declared scope; named log/fax targets recorded.
+- [x] Distinguish facts, source reports, inference and unknowns: README observations, assessment and provenance; no manufactured conflict or motive finding.
+- [x] Test contrary interpretation: log instruction and reported event support review activity; no claim that no review occurred.
+- [x] Missing inputs remain TODOs: OPEN-TODOS.json, with original eighteen requirements retained.
+- [x] Avoid duplicate acquisition/testing: held interview/renders reused, named queries checked against holdings; no raw-data test claimed.
+- [x] Exact locators: source URL, access date, page/row/mark; native log hash explicitly unknown. No invented source lines.
+- [x] Actual scope: twelve log viewports plus held pages8–9. Truncated initial page9 display corrected by reinspection, not silently counted as a reading.
+- [x] Revision accountability: new text only, immediate predecessor absent. TEXT-CHANGES.diff is a real Git addition diff; source-image reading is separate.
+- [x] Public payload review: research notes only; raw sources, incidental personal/access fields, other marked material and private case content excluded.
+- [ ] Commit/push/remote verification: performed and recorded separately after freezing this candidate; this checklist does not prejudge publication success.
+
+Integrity checks identify held bytes, not historical truth, independent validation or completion of the substantive goal. No prior discrepancy has been resolved or erased by this supplement.
