+# SOCC follow-up: named review and message-transfer records remain unacquired
+
+Research date: October 31, 2026. Existing parent tasks: TEL02/TEL04, AUD016-A1 and TC05–TC06. This is a bounded continuation of the recording-retrieval inquiry, separate from the [completed exhibits 336/337 comparison](https://github.com/AveLyra/911-conspiracy-investigation/blob/385f959fd70d5caee75fe192325771ed7d8bdc9d/investigation/broader-evidence/moussaoui-french-controls-2026-10-30/README.md). Earlier reports, conflicting values and source copies remain unchanged.
+
+Two additional entries identify specific records to seek. They do not establish the disposition of the earlier recordings. The distinction between an instruction, a later recollection, an actual document and proof of receipt is material here.
+
+## Observations and source roles
+
+| Source and exact locator | What the readable source reports | What remains unverified |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| [SOCC log mirror, viewer page 20](https://www.scribd.com/document/16762194/T7-B20-Timelines-9-11-2-of-2-Fdr-AA-SOCC-Log-Redacted-Version#page=20), September 17 divider, row **0955**, production mark **AA KEAN COMM 002549** | Announcement to start an informal lessons-learned log, to be addressed upon SOCC closure | The actual log, its completion, contributors, closure discussion, action list and any recording-preservation entry |
+| [Held November 19, 2003 interview memorandum, physical page 8](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialive/0/6096/2609600/content/arcmedia/9-11/MFR/t-0148-911MFR-00014.pdf#page=8), **Recommendations**, first paragraph marked [U] | Interviewees reportedly described an after-action lessons-learned event, including SOCC response and principally the new hijacking strategy; they also reported that PTI/SOCC activation systems did not change | Actual event materials, attendance, decisions and implementation. This is a retrospective memorandum, not the informal log itself |
+| [SOCC log mirror, viewer page 22](https://www.scribd.com/document/16762194/T7-B20-Timelines-9-11-2-of-2-Fdr-AA-SOCC-Log-Redacted-Version#page=22), September 18 divider, rows **1135**, **1138** and **1220**, mark **AA KEAN COMM 002551** | Earlier rows report an unconfirmed hijack message followed by all-OK; row 1220 reports an FAA ATC Command Center request for that message, approval and a fax to a masked recipient | Original message, authorization/routing, actual fax, delivery and acknowledgment. The later all-OK account must accompany the initial report |
+
+The fax entry concerns a **September 18 event**, not September 11 recordings and not the May 2003 corrected FAA answer. No masked recipient was reconstructed. A source's report that something was faxed is not an independently verified delivery receipt. Likewise, similar lessons-learned wording does not establish that the September 17 proposed log and the later reported event were the same object or that one implemented the other.
+
+## Assessment, counterevidence and limits
+
+The new entries sharpen retrieval targets: a named informal log, closure/debrief records and a particular message-transfer chain. They provide no newly acquired recording, native call data, laboratory result or signed FAA disposition. The interview was already acquired and read in the earlier study; reusing it is **not a new source acquisition or independent corroboration**.
+
+The instruction and later reported event are evidence or accounts of review activity. They weigh against a blanket claim that no review effort occurred. They do not establish that recording preservation was addressed, recommendations were implemented, or communications were effective. Different scope, incomplete implementation and an informal log not identical to the later event remain untested possibilities. No contradiction between these entries is established, and no suppression, coordination, intent or conspiracy is inferred from a missing record.
+
+The recording-outcome check found **no explicit disposition of the earlier retrieval request in the readable regions of pages 19–24**. That is not an absence finding for the entire 32-page log, redacted fields, other files or historical events. [READING-SCOPE.json](READING-SCOPE.json) preserves the actual page regions and limits. No new scientific or historical-action test was performed; all eighteen original-record requirements remain open or partial.
+
+## Provenance and actual work
+
+The log was inspected through a public mirror: twelve viewport images, two overlapping regions per page, pages 19–24 only. Date dividers, row labels and footer marks were preserved as displayed, without clock or document-creation authentication. Faint embedded details and masks remain unreadable/unverified. No native log PDF was acquired, so its native PDF SHA-256 is **unknown**, not substituted with a hash of these notes.
+
+The already-held interview PDF has nine physical pages and SHA-256 **e45e7435e80b81df3f0c0376fb7be049595c1653dc6a00f1b6718c1b7dd411b3**. Physical pages 8–9 were reinspected from existing renders; page 9 continues a separate example and supplies no actual informal log or recording disposition. Only the relevant [U] paragraph on page 8 is summarized here. Other marked material and raw images are excluded. The agency-hosted PDF was acquired previously through a tested legacy-path candidate; it was not newly located through an observed catalog download link in this unit.
+
+Two prospectively defined searches for the named log/event returned the already-held interview and an indexed excerpts mirror. No informal log, event minutes/slides or fax receipt was acquired. Excerpts reusing the interview are not another independent source. The query misses do not establish that records do not exist. No extra log pages or hidden layers were inspected.
+
+[OPEN-TODOS.json](OPEN-TODOS.json) retains the missing inputs, competing outcomes and next discriminating tests. [SOURCE-PINS.json](SOURCE-PINS.json) separates mirror observations from the held agency-hosted copy. [VALIDATION.json](VALIDATION.json) records mechanical integrity checks only. [CHECKLIST.md](CHECKLIST.md) and [TEXT-CHANGES.diff](TEXT-CHANGES.diff) provide revision accountability; the latter is the actual addition diff against the preceding absent text state, not a source-document version comparison.
+
+Publication covers original research notes only. No raw scans, screenshots, full OCR, contact/access-code/passenger data, private correspondence, case strategy or credentials are included. Source originals, masks, page order, earlier conflicting records and prior TODOs are retained. No outreach, request, fee, filing, deletion, private push, merge or history rewrite was performed. Publication and remote integrity are separate from substantive research acceptance.
